WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.110
- [Narrator] Thanks to Dashlane,

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:03.163
for keeping Legal Eagle in the air.

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:07.963
- I'm gonna make this pencil disappear.

00:00:10.295 --> 00:00:11.780
Ta-da!

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:14.453
- Cute magic trick, also
first degree murder.

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:21.690
Hey Legal Eagles, it's time
to think like a lawyer.

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:23.100
Welcome back to Laws Broken

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:26.230
where an attorney destroys
your favorite childhood movies

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:29.030
by showing you how illegal everything is.

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:31.380
Because everything is illegal.

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:33.250
This week we're going to
examine The Dark Knight

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:35.320
and we're finally going
to answer the question,

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:38.500
can Batman use the
self-defense justification?

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:39.500
Can you trust me?

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:40.850
- Do you trust him?

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:42.880
- Of course you can trust
me, I'm an attorney.

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:45.010
As most people know, the
Batman stories take place

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:46.730
in the fictional city of Gotham,

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:49.010
but as everyone recognizes, Gotham is just

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:52.130
a stand in for New York
City and since I am licensed

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:53.770
to practice in the state of New York,

00:00:53.770 --> 00:00:56.050
I'm going to be using New
York law for the most part

00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:59.290
to talk about the various
crimes of the Joker and Batman.

00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:01.400
So, be sure to subscribe and comment

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.170
in the form of an objection which I'll

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:05.970
either sustain or
overrule and stick around

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:06.950
until the end of the video

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:08.560
where I give a verdict for how long

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:12.710
the Joker and Batman
are both going to jail.

00:01:12.710 --> 00:01:14.900
So, let's examine the evidence.

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:17.400
(tense music)

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:25.850
Alright so we have your standard,

00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:27.580
garden-variety breaking and entering

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:31.000
and criminal trespass onto
the building of a bank.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.390
- Three of a kind, let's do this.

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:33.760
- That's it, three guys?

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:36.210
- Two guys on the roof,
every guy gets a share,

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:37.470
five shares is plenty.

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:39.920
- Six shares, don't forget
the guy who planned the job.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:41.070
- He thinks he can sit it out

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:42.350
and still take a slice.

00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:44.740
I know why they call him the Joker.

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:46.970
- Okay, so these bad guys
have helpfully explained

00:01:46.970 --> 00:01:49.240
that they are all engaged
in a criminal conspiracy

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:50.480
to rob a bank.

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:52.410
As members of a conspiracy, assuming

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:54.420
that the Pinkerton Doctrine applies,

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:57.130
all of the members of the
conspiracy including the Joker

00:01:57.130 --> 00:01:59.210
are on the hook for all
of the criminal acts

00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:00.470
of their co-conspirators.

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:03.760
So, I'm going to impute all
of the bank robbers bad acts

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:05.343
to the Joker himself.

00:02:05.343 --> 00:02:06.989
(general shouting)

00:02:06.989 --> 00:02:08.529
(woman screaming)

00:02:08.529 --> 00:02:10.924
- [Clown] I said stay down there.

00:02:10.924 --> 00:02:12.330
- That's funny, it didn't dial out to 911,

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:13.990
it was trying to reach a private number.

00:02:13.990 --> 00:02:14.823
- Is there a problem?

00:02:14.823 --> 00:02:16.660
- No, I'm done here.

00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:18.900
- And that's just straight up murder

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:20.450
but because all of these bank robbers

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:22.650
are engaged in a conspiracy to conduct

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:26.170
an inherently dangerous
crime, that's armed robbery,

00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:28.686
with guns, and bombs, and grenades,

00:02:28.686 --> 00:02:31.940
all of those co-conspirators
are likely on the hook

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:34.950
for the murder of this person
under the felony murder rule.

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:36.800
But on top of that, the felony murder rule

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:38.900
would apply to any unintentional killings

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:41.850
that occur during the course
of this armed robbery as well.

00:02:42.828 --> 00:02:45.100
- [Clown] Nobody make a
move, nobody, stay down!

00:02:46.375 --> 00:02:48.542
(gunshot)

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:54.313
- Alright William Fichtner
bringing the heat.

00:02:55.889 --> 00:02:58.056
(gunshot)

00:02:58.910 --> 00:03:01.640
So, the bank manager comes
out with guns blazing.

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:04.100
You might assume that
this is attempted murder

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:05.500
because he's using a shotgun to try

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:07.650
and kill the bank robbers, but it's likely

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:10.650
that the justification of
self defense applies here

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:12.910
and excuses his actions.

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:14.440
We're gonna be talking a lot about

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:16.790
the justification of
self defense in a moment

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:19.360
but to give you a
preview, robbery is one of

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:21.560
the enumerated categories of situations

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:23.880
where you're allowed to use deadly force

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:25.140
to protect against it.

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:27.160
So, I think the bank manager
is probably justified

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:29.190
in using deadly force to protect against

00:03:29.190 --> 00:03:31.290
the robbery of the Joker and his henchmen.

00:03:32.939 --> 00:03:34.950
(machine gun firing)

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:37.050
And because the Joker is not justified

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:38.040
in using deadly force,

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:40.790
that's just plain old attempted murder.

00:03:40.790 --> 00:03:43.700
- Boss told me when the guy was
done, I should take him out.

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:44.813
One less share, right.

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:48.690
- Funny, he told me something similar.

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:49.523
- What?

00:03:49.523 --> 00:03:50.910
No, no, no!

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:51.840
- More murder.

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:53.880
- [Clown] I'm bettin' the
Joker told you to kill me

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:55.653
soon as we loaded the cash.

00:03:56.660 --> 00:03:59.563
- No, no, no, no, I kill the bus driver.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:02.033
- Bus driver?

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:05.513
What bus driver?

00:04:07.690 --> 00:04:10.080
- Obviously this is
some type of murder here

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:11.280
but what's going on?

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:14.070
Well, the Joker knew that
bus was going to break

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:15.900
through the wall at a certain time.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:19.230
So one might argue that
because he didn't intentionally

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:21.020
pull a trigger and shoot a gun,

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:23.200
that he's not liable
for first degree murder.

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:25.010
The problem is that because he knew

00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:27.490
this was going to happen
and moved out of the way

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:30.410
and forced the guy into
the path of the bus,

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:32.440
that is a mental state we call knowingly

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:34.960
which generally carries with
it exactly the same kind

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:37.808
of penalty that you would
have when you intentionally

00:04:37.808 --> 00:04:40.600
do an act that results in someone's death.

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:42.240
So, in this case, even
though the Joker didn't pull

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:44.730
the trigger, he knowingly engaged

00:04:44.730 --> 00:04:46.700
in actions that would lead to the death

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:48.840
of his co-conspirator
which would qualify as

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:51.810
at least second degree murder,
if not first degree murder.

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:53.010
- That's a lot of money.

00:04:56.960 --> 00:04:58.764
What happened to the rest of the guys?

00:04:58.764 --> 00:05:00.430
(machine gun fires)

00:05:00.430 --> 00:05:03.230
- And that's just your garden
variety form of murder.

00:05:03.230 --> 00:05:04.381
- [Bank Manager] Look at you.

00:05:04.381 --> 00:05:05.925
What do you believe in, huh?

00:05:05.925 --> 00:05:07.370
What do you believe in?

00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:10.060
- [Joker] I believe,
whatever doesn't kill you,

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:14.403
simply makes you stranger.

00:05:15.297 --> 00:05:18.640
- So the Joker made physical
contact with the bank manager

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:21.230
there which technically
qualifies as assault

00:05:21.230 --> 00:05:23.900
and because he used a smoke bomb instead

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:26.300
of an actual incendiary grenade,

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:27.320
I think that would probably qualify

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:29.860
as intentional infliction
of emotional distress,

00:05:29.860 --> 00:05:32.160
even though the man was
not physically harmed

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:33.963
in the explosion from a grenade.

00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:37.990
(glass shattering)

00:05:37.990 --> 00:05:39.293
Destruction of property.

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:43.200
- Don't let me find you out here again.

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:44.830
- We're trying to help you.

00:05:44.830 --> 00:05:46.020
- I don't need help!

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:47.530
- Not my diagnosis.

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:49.210
- What gives you the right?

00:05:49.210 --> 00:05:51.480
What's the difference between you and me?

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:52.460
- Not much.

00:05:52.460 --> 00:05:55.130
Is Batman justified in using self-defense

00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:57.090
and patrolling the streets of Gotham?

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:58.938
Well, let's think like a lawyer.

00:05:58.938 --> 00:06:01.820
(intense rock music)

00:06:01.820 --> 00:06:04.500
The state of New York
recognizes self-defense

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:07.690
as a justification for
using physical force

00:06:07.690 --> 00:06:09.960
in the defense of different people.

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:12.290
Whether it applies is complicated.

00:06:12.290 --> 00:06:14.540
Now, the rules of using physical force

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:16.960
and deadly physical force are different.

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:18.180
Generally speaking, you're allowed

00:06:18.180 --> 00:06:21.030
to use physical force in self defense

00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:22.890
if you believe it is reasonably necessary

00:06:22.890 --> 00:06:26.070
to defend yourself or
a third person against

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:28.900
the imminent use of
unlawful physical force.

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:30.310
Of course, there are exceptions to that.

00:06:30.310 --> 00:06:33.160
You are not justified
in using physical force

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:36.450
when your conduct is the
one that provoked the actor

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:38.220
who is going to use
physical force against you.

00:06:38.220 --> 00:06:39.790
You can't use physical force if you

00:06:39.790 --> 00:06:43.340
were the initial aggressor
unless you have clearly

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:45.610
withdrawn from the
encounter and communicated

00:06:45.610 --> 00:06:48.110
that you have withdrawn
and the second person

00:06:48.110 --> 00:06:50.000
has continued to attack you.

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:52.590
Now, the rules of using
deadly force are even

00:06:52.590 --> 00:06:54.950
more strict than using
just physical force.

00:06:54.950 --> 00:06:57.100
You are not allowed to use deadly force

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:59.470
unless you reasonably believe
that the other aggressor

00:06:59.470 --> 00:07:02.150
is in fact going to use
deadly force against you

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:03.760
and that is your option to prevent

00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:05.240
it being used against yourself.

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:08.040
But even there, if you
have the opportunity

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:11.260
to avoid the situation
entirely and retreat to safety,

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:13.420
you have an obligation to do so

00:07:13.420 --> 00:07:16.000
before engaging in deadly force.

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:19.040
However, you don't have a
duty to withdraw if you are,

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:21.970
one, in your own home
or two, you reasonably

00:07:21.970 --> 00:07:24.830
believe that another person
is attempting to commit

00:07:24.830 --> 00:07:28.010
a burglary or you believe that
the aggressive third party

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:30.680
who is bout to use deadly force is going

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:33.220
to commit a kidnapping, a forcible rape,

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:36.780
a forcible criminal sexual
assault, or a robbery.

00:07:36.780 --> 00:07:39.850
Under those specific
enumerated situations,

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:42.070
you don't have a duty to retreat.

00:07:42.070 --> 00:07:44.131
How do we deal with Batman?

00:07:44.131 --> 00:07:44.964
I'm Batman.

00:07:44.964 --> 00:07:46.470
Well, number one, I don't think Batman

00:07:46.470 --> 00:07:48.130
is ever using regular physical force.

00:07:48.130 --> 00:07:50.570
He has been trained as basically a ninja.

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:53.270
While he has a code that says
he shouldn't kill someone,

00:07:53.270 --> 00:07:55.490
he has the kind of training that makes

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:58.320
his actions, I think,
deadly and, even though

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:00.360
he doesn't try to kill
people, I think it's clear

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:02.550
that people die when he gets involved.

00:08:02.550 --> 00:08:05.160
We can disagree about whether
his acts are on balance

00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:07.260
good for the city but
the fact of the matter is

00:08:07.260 --> 00:08:09.700
they are illegal, at
least under New York law.

00:08:09.700 --> 00:08:12.580
New York law does not
look kindly on vigilantes.

00:08:12.580 --> 00:08:15.960
You can't just interject
yourself into crime

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:17.980
and pretend to be police.

00:08:17.980 --> 00:08:19.300
It just doesn't work that way.

00:08:19.300 --> 00:08:21.520
He would likely be on the hook as guilty

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:24.770
for all of the hundreds of
acts of physical assault

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:28.130
that he has committed again
the criminals of Gotham.

00:08:28.130 --> 00:08:30.260
(slamming noise)

00:08:30.260 --> 00:08:32.610
- [Joker] I'm gonna make
this pencil disappear.

00:08:34.901 --> 00:08:36.410
Ta-da!

00:08:36.410 --> 00:08:39.890
- Cute magic trick, also
first degree murder.

00:08:39.890 --> 00:08:41.836
- Enough from the clown!

00:08:41.836 --> 00:08:46.836
- (tuts smugly) Let's not
blow this out of proportion.

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:48.850
- Alright, threatening everyone

00:08:48.850 --> 00:08:51.200
with a jacket full of grenades.

00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:53.270
That's what we call a true threat.

00:08:53.270 --> 00:08:55.700
Sometimes you run into
first amendment issues

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:57.930
and whether you're allowed to
say things to certain people.

00:08:57.930 --> 00:09:01.420
That's clearly not allowed
here where you have

00:09:01.420 --> 00:09:03.070
what are presumably real grenades

00:09:03.070 --> 00:09:04.720
and threatening people with them.

00:09:06.170 --> 00:09:07.173
- Why so serious?

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:12.860
- Alright, so there's some regular murder.

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:17.070
- [Joker] Now, our operation is small but

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:22.070
there is a lot of potential
for aggressive expansion

00:09:22.730 --> 00:09:25.980
so which of you fine gentlemen
would like to join our team?

00:09:25.980 --> 00:09:28.760
Oh, there's only one spot open right now

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:33.190
so we're gonna have tryouts.

00:09:33.190 --> 00:09:35.550
- Arguably you could say
that those people engaged

00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:38.710
in physical violence because
of the duress from the Joker

00:09:38.710 --> 00:09:40.280
so I think the Joker's
probably on the hook

00:09:40.280 --> 00:09:43.269
for two more counts of homicide.

00:09:43.269 --> 00:09:45.769
(tense music)

00:09:54.540 --> 00:09:57.030
I'm not sure what the
equivalent of the FAA would be

00:09:57.030 --> 00:09:59.590
in Hong Kong but you're not allowed

00:09:59.590 --> 00:10:02.110
to go gliding around a city like that.

00:10:02.110 --> 00:10:04.950
That would be a violation
of airspace, at least

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:07.170
in New York City, I'm
assuming Hong Kong probably

00:10:07.170 --> 00:10:08.270
has a similar thing.

00:10:08.270 --> 00:10:10.360
So when people go base
jumping off of buildings,

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:12.380
totally illegal, reckless endangerment

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:16.058
and some sort of
violation of aviation law.

00:10:16.058 --> 00:10:19.975
(shouting in foreign language)

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:34.330
And there Batman just
straight up kidnaps Lao,

00:10:34.330 --> 00:10:36.260
whatever the Hong Kong
equivalent of kidnapping,

00:10:36.260 --> 00:10:39.342
I think that's probably what
that man just engaged in.

00:10:39.342 --> 00:10:42.630
(tense music)

00:10:42.630 --> 00:10:46.070
Batman drops off Lao to Lieutenant Gordon.

00:10:46.070 --> 00:10:47.950
So the question is, can the police

00:10:47.950 --> 00:10:50.800
actually use evidence
that they get from Lao

00:10:50.800 --> 00:10:53.570
because Batman illegally kidnapped him

00:10:53.570 --> 00:10:55.310
from an international country?

00:10:55.310 --> 00:10:57.590
Well, there is a doctrine that applies

00:10:57.590 --> 00:10:59.440
to governments that says,

00:10:59.440 --> 00:11:02.090
if the evidence is wrongfully obtained

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:04.200
and you use that wrongfully
obtained evidence

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:06.500
to find more evidence down the line,

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:08.420
that's called the fruit
of the poisonous tree

00:11:08.420 --> 00:11:10.820
and often that is excluded at trial.

00:11:10.820 --> 00:11:13.580
But the thing is, Batman
is not a police officer.

00:11:13.580 --> 00:11:15.290
Batman is a private party.

00:11:15.290 --> 00:11:17.700
So, while Batman may be liable

00:11:17.700 --> 00:11:19.590
and almost certainly is liable for the use

00:11:19.590 --> 00:11:22.520
of deadly force and
for illegal kidnapping,

00:11:22.520 --> 00:11:25.340
the fruit of the poisonous
tree doctrine doesn't apply

00:11:25.340 --> 00:11:27.650
because the police here were blameless.

00:11:27.650 --> 00:11:29.770
- 'Cause they get anything on you

00:11:29.770 --> 00:11:32.640
and those criminals are
back on the streets,

00:11:32.640 --> 00:11:34.203
followed swiftly by you and me.

00:11:36.010 --> 00:11:39.860
- Alright, another act
of murder by the Joker.

00:11:39.860 --> 00:11:42.283
Killing the Batman-like vigilante.

00:11:45.380 --> 00:11:49.080
- You see, this is how
crazy Batman's made Gotham.

00:11:49.080 --> 00:11:52.790
You want order in Gotham,
the Batman must take off

00:11:52.790 --> 00:11:55.293
his mask and turn himself in.

00:11:56.350 --> 00:11:59.023
Oh, and every day he
doesn't, people will die.

00:12:00.390 --> 00:12:04.363
Starting tonight, I'm a man of my word.

00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:08.500
(maniacal laughter)

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:11.850
- Alright, so the Joker
there not only is he engaging

00:12:11.850 --> 00:12:13.590
in assault and homicide against

00:12:13.590 --> 00:12:17.760
this vigilante Batman wannabe,
but he's also engaging

